2021-06-30", "flag": "verified", "claim_id": "c097"}, {"text": "The mouth works' recorded progression: curved training walls under progress in the state's status report of 1 February 2024; 95% complete in WRD's Policy Note 2024-25; 'all Works have been Completed' in the 2025-26 note.", "source": "CRRT status report to the NGT (01.02.2024); WRD Policy Notes 2024-25 and 2025-26", "date": "2024-2025", "flag": "verified", "claim_id": "c098"}, {"text": "PWD's own record lists twelve schemes for sustained opening of the mouth between 1890 and 2000, from staged groynes to a 400 m tidal weir proposed at Napier Bridge in 1922.", "source": "CMDA Seminar on Waterways in Chennai, Session III", "date": "2010-03", "flag": "verified", "claim_id": "c099"}]}}